{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"case-rename","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Case Rename","description":"Rename a name in every naming style at once (userName, UserName, user_name, user-name, USER_NAME) with a dry-run preview.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:caseRename.rename","onCommand:caseRename.convert"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"caseRename.rename","title":"Rename in All Naming Styles...","category":"Case Rename"},{"command":"caseRename.convert","title":"Write Name Under Cursor in Another Style...","category":"Case Rename"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"caseRename.rename","key":"Ctrl+Alt+R"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Case Rename: rename an identifier in every naming style at once (userName, UserName, user_name, user-name, USER_NAME),\n// after a dry-run preview that lists every change before anything is touched.\n\nfunction words(s) {\n  return s\n    .replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1 $2')\n    .replace(/([A-Z]+)([A-Z][a-z])/g, '$1 $2')\n    .split(/[^A-Za-z0-9]+/)\n    .filter(Boolean);\n}\nconst cap = (w) => w.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + w.slice(1).toLowerCase();\nconst forms = (name) => {\n  const w = words(name);\n  if (!w.length) return null;\n  return {\n    camel: w.map((x, i) => (i ? cap(x) : x.toLowerCase())).join(''),\n    pascal: w.map(cap).join(''),\n    snake: w.map((x) => x.toLowerCase()).join('_'),\n    kebab: w.map((x) => x.toLowerCase()).join('-'),\n    constant: w.map((x) => x.toUpperCase()).join('_'),\n  };\n};\nconst escRe = (s) => s.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');\n\n/** The text pairs to replace: every naming style of the old name mapped to the same style of the new name. */\nfunction pairs(oldName, newName) {\n  const a = forms(oldName);\n  const b = forms(newName);\n  if (!a || !b) return [];\n  const out = new Map();\n  for (const k of Object.keys(a)) if (a[k] && a[k] !== b[k] && !out.has(a[k])) out.set(a[k], { to: b[k], style: k });\n  return [...out.entries()].map(([from, v]) => ({ from, to: v.to, style: v.style }));\n}\n\n/**\n * Plans the edits. `inside` also renames the name when it is a part of a longer identifier (getUserName, MAX_USER_NAME).\n * Returns [{ line, col, from, to, style }] sorted by position.\n */\nfunction plan(text, oldName, newName, inside) {\n  const list = pairs(oldName, newName);\n  const found = [];\n  const lines = text.split('\\n');\n  for (const p of list) {\n    let re;\n    if (!inside) re = new RegExp('(?<![A-Za-z0-9_$])' + escRe(p.from) + '(?![A-Za-z0-9_$])', 'g');\n    else if (p.style === 'pascal') re = new RegExp(escRe(p.from) + '(?![a-z])', 'g');\n    else if (p.style === 'camel') re = new RegExp('(?<![A-Za-z0-9_$])' + escRe(p.from) + '(?![a-z0-9])', 'g');\n    else re = new RegExp('(?<![A-Za-z0-9])' + escRe(p.from) + '(?![A-Za-z0-9])', 'g');\n    lines.forEach((line, i) => {\n      let m;\n      while ((m = re.exec(line))) {\n        found.push({ line: i, col: m.index, from: p.from, to: p.to, style: p.style });\n        if (m[0].length === 0) re.lastIndex++;\n      }\n    });\n  }\n  found.sort((x, y) => x.line - y.line || x.col - y.col);\n  // Two styles can match the same spot (a one word name); keep the first.\n  return found.filter((e, i) => !(i && found[i - 1].line === e.line && found[i - 1].col === e.col));\n}\n\nfunction apply(text, edits) {\n  const lines = text.split('\\n');\n  for (const e of [...edits].sort((x, y) => y.line - x.line || y.col - x.col)) lines[e.line] = lines[e.line].slice(0, e.col) + e.to + lines[e.line].slice(e.col + e.from.length);\n  return lines.join('\\n');\n}\n\nconst esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\n\nfunction preview(oldName, newName, edits, lines, inside) {\n  const rows = edits\n    .slice(0, 400)\n    .map((e) => {\n      const line = lines[e.line];\n      const before = esc(line.slice(0, e.col)) + '<mark class=\"o\">' + esc(e.from) + '</mark>' + esc(line.slice(e.col + e.from.length));\n      const after = esc(line.slice(0, e.col)) + '<mark class=\"n\">' + esc(e.to) + '</mark>' + esc(line.slice(e.col + e.from.length));\n      return `<tr data-l=\"${e.line}\"><td class=\"ln\">${e.line + 1}</td><td><div class=\"b\">${before}</div><div class=\"a\">${after}</div></td></tr>`;\n    })\n    .join('');\n  const styles = {};\n  for (const e of edits) styles[e.style] = (styles[e.style] || 0) + 1;\n  const chips = Object.entries(styles).map(([k, n]) => `<span class=\"chip\">${k} ${n}</span>`).join('');\n  return `<style>\n  body { font-family: var(--ui); } h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; } .dim { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 12px; }\n  .top { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; margin: 12px 0; } .top .sp { flex: 1; }\n  button { background: var(--raised, transparent); color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; padding: 5px 12px; cursor: pointer; } button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }\n  button.go { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border-color: var(--accent); } button:disabled { opacity: .4; cursor: default; }\n  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font: 12px/1.5 var(--mono, monospace); } td { padding: 4px 8px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; } .ln { color: var(--fg-dim); width: 40px; text-align: right; }\n  .b, .a { white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; } .b { opacity: .75; } mark.o { background: rgba(239,68,68,.35); color: inherit; } mark.n { background: rgba(34,197,94,.35); color: inherit; }\n  .chip { display: inline-block; background: var(--raised, rgba(128,128,128,.2)); padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 11px; margin-right: 6px; }\n</style>\n<h3>Rename ${esc(oldName)} to ${esc(newName)}</h3>\n<div class=\"dim\">Dry run: nothing has been changed yet. ${inside ? 'Also renaming inside longer names.' : 'Whole names only.'}</div>\n<div class=\"top\"><b>${edits.length} change${edits.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}</b>${chips}<span class=\"sp\"></span><button id=\"cancel\">Cancel</button><button id=\"go\" class=\"go\"${edits.length ? '' : ' disabled'}>Apply ${edits.length}</button></div>\n<table>${rows || '<tr><td>Nothing to rename.</td></tr>'}</table>${edits.length > 400 ? '<p class=\"dim\">Showing the first 400 of ' + edits.length + '. Apply changes all of them.</p>' : ''}\n<script>\n  document.getElementById('cancel').onclick = () => ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'cancel' });\n  document.getElementById('go').onclick = () => ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'apply' });\n</script>`;\n}\n\nexports._test = { words, forms, pairs, plan, apply };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let panel = null;\n  let pending = null;\n\n  /** The name to rename: the selection, or the word under the cursor. */\n  async function target(doc) {\n    if (doc.selectedText && /^[A-Za-z0-9_$-]+$/.test(doc.selectedText.trim())) return doc.selectedText.trim();\n    const line = await ferrum.editor.getLine(doc.selection.start.line);\n    const col = doc.selection.start.col;\n    const left = /[A-Za-z0-9_$-]*$/.exec(line.slice(0, col))[0];\n    const right = /^[A-Za-z0-9_$-]*/.exec(line.slice(col))[0];\n    return (left + right).replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '');\n  }\n\n  async function run() {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file first.', 'warn');\n    const oldName = await target(doc);\n    if (!oldName) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Put the cursor on a name, or select it.', 'warn');\n    const newName = (await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Rename \"' + oldName + '\" to', value: oldName }) || '').trim();\n    if (!newName || newName === oldName) return;\n    if (!words(newName).length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The new name needs letters or digits.', 'warn');\n    const mode = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(\n      [{ label: 'Whole names only', detail: 'userName, user_name, UserName, USER_NAME. Longer names that only contain it are left alone.', inside: false }, { label: 'Also inside longer names', detail: 'Also getUserName, MAX_USER_NAME, user_name_list.', inside: true }],\n      { placeholder: 'What should be renamed?' },\n    );\n    if (!mode) return;\n    const lines = doc.text.split('\\n');\n    const edits = plan(doc.text, oldName, newName, mode.inside);\n    const html = preview(oldName, newName, edits, lines, mode.inside);\n    pending = { text: doc.text, edits };\n    if (panel) panel.setHtml(html);\n    else {\n      panel = await ferrum.window.showPanel({ title: 'Rename preview', html });\n      panel.onDidClose(() => (panel = null));\n      panel.onMessage(async (m) => {\n        if (m.type !== 'apply' || !pending) return;\n        const job = pending;\n        pending = null;\n        const now = await ferrum.editor.active();\n        if (!now || now.text !== job.text) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The file changed since the preview. Run the rename again.', 'warn');\n        await ferrum.editor.edit(job.edits.map((e) => ({ range: { start: { line: e.line, col: e.col }, end: { line: e.line, col: e.col + e.from.length } }, text: e.to })));\n        ferrum.window.showMessage('Renamed ' + job.edits.length + ' place' + (job.edits.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + '. Undo brings it all back at once.');\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('caseRename.rename', run),\n    ferrum.commands.register('caseRename.convert', async () => {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file first.', 'warn');\n      const name = await target(doc);\n      if (!name) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Put the cursor on a name, or select it.', 'warn');\n      const f = forms(name);\n      if (!f) return;\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.entries(f).map(([k, v]) => ({ label: v, detail: k })), { placeholder: 'Write \"' + name + '\" as...' });\n      if (!pick) return;\n      if (doc.selectedText) return ferrum.editor.insert(pick.label);\n      const line = await ferrum.editor.getLine(doc.selection.start.line);\n      const col = doc.selection.start.col;\n      const left = /[A-Za-z0-9_$-]*$/.exec(line.slice(0, col))[0];\n      await ferrum.editor.replace({ start: { line: doc.selection.start.line, col: col - left.length }, end: { line: doc.selection.start.line, col: col - left.length + name.length } }, pick.label);\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Case Rename\n\nRename a variable, function, class or constant **in every naming style at once**. Put the cursor on `userName`, run **Rename in All Naming Styles...**, type `accountName`, and `userName`, `UserName`, `user_name`, `user-name` and `USER_NAME` all change to the matching style of the new name.\n\n## Dry run first\n\nBefore anything changes, a preview panel lists **every change** with the line before and after and a count per style. Nothing is touched until you press **Apply**. The change is one undo step. If the file changed while you looked at the preview, it refuses to apply and asks you to run it again.\n\n## Two modes\n\n- **Whole names only**: `userName` is renamed but `getUserName` is left alone.\n- **Also inside longer names**: `getUserName`, `MAX_USER_NAME` and `user_name_list` change too.\n\n## Also\n\n**Write Name Under Cursor in Another Style...** converts one name to camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case, kebab-case or CONSTANT_CASE.\n\nIt works on the file you have open. For a rename across many files, use **Search in Files** to look first.\n\nNo permissions needed.\n"}}}